-objects"><title>Figures and Tables</title><fig id="pone-0000438-g001" position="float"><object-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1371/journal.pone.0000438.g001</object-id><label>Figure 1</label><caption><title>Proportion of 454 pyrosequencing DNA fragments that exhibited SNPs.</title><p>No match indicates a DNA fragment not from <italic>M. mulatta</italic>. A near match indicates a DNA fragment with at least a 98&#x00025; match to <italic>M. mulatta</italic> but unsuitable for SNP detection. A perfect match indicates a DNA fragment with a 100&#x00025; match with <italic>M. mulatta</italic>. A SNP indicates a DNA fragment with a near perfect match with <italic>M. mulatta</italic> and suitable sequence for SNP detection.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="pone.0000438.g001"/></fig><fig id="pone-0000438-g002" position="float"><object-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1371/journal.pone.0000438.g002</object-id><label>Figure 2</label><caption><title>Distribution of Candidate SNPs across genome.</title></caption><graphic xlink:href="pone.0000438.g002"/></fig><fig id="pone-0000438-g003" position="float"><object-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1371/journal.pone.0000438.g003</object-id><label>Figure 3</label><caption><title>Distribution of overlap SNPs across the genome.</title></caption><graphic xlink:href="pone.0000438.g003"/></fig><table-wrap id="pone-0000438-t001" position="float"><object-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1371/journal.pone.0000438.t001</object-id><label>Table 1</label><caption><title>Candidate SNPs confirmed through Sanger sequencing.</title></caption><graphic id="pone-0000438-t001-1" xlink:href="pone.0000438.t001"/><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" alternate-form-of="pone-0000438-t001-1"><colgroup span="1"><col align="left" span="1"/><col align="center" span="1"/><col align="center" span="1"/><col align="center" span="1"/><col align="center" span="1"/><col align="center" span="1"/><col align="center" span="1"/></colgroup><thead><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td align="left